      <div class="section-header reveal">
        <span class="section-tag">Cultural Overview</span>
        <h2>Understanding Tanzania's Tribal Diversity</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-content reveal">
        <p>Tanzania is home to over <strong>120 ethnic groups</strong>, each with distinct languages, traditions, and customs. This cultural richness is one of East Africa's greatest assets. While the Maasai are internationally famous, they represent just one thread in a vibrant tapestry.</p>
        <p>On Zanzibar specifically, the dominant culture is <strong>Swahili</strong> — a unique blend of African, Arab, Persian, and Indian influences shaped by centuries of Indian Ocean trade. The Swahili language (Kiswahili) itself emerged as a coastal trading lingua franca and is now Tanzania's national language.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

