            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: #4e5d66; line-height: 1.5;">Semi-nomadic pastoralists famous for their distinctive red shukas, intricate beadwork, and jumping dances (adumu). Cattle are central to their economy, social status, and spiritual life. Many Maasai communities welcome visitors to their bomas (homesteads) for cultural exchanges — look for community-run programs that directly benefit local families.</p>
            <ul class="tribe-highlights">
              <li>Population: ~1.2 million</li>
              <li>Language: Maa</li>
              <li>Key experience: Village visit, warrior dance</li>
            </ul>
